WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Step 1: In Google Cloud open IAM and Admin, Service Accounts, Create service account. Add a JSON key and note its numeric client ID.

2
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Step 2: In admin.google.com as a super admin: Security, Access and data control, API controls, Manage domain-wide delegation.

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Step 3: Click Add new.

4
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Step 4: Paste the service account's numeric client ID, not its email.

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Step 5: Paste gmail.send, gmail.modify and calendar, comma separated. Invites need calendar; cold email needs the two Gmail scopes.

6
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Step 6: Click Authorise. One entry covers every mailbox in that Workspace.

7
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Step 7: In Tantra open Connectors, Google Service Accounts.

8
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Step 8: Drop the JSON key here, up to 30 at once, add a tag and click Upload. Tantra stores it encrypted.

9
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Step 9: On Accounts, paste every mailbox in that Workspace and click Verify & Add.

10
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Step 10: Each one should show Connected and Gmail capable. Calendar-only means the Gmail scopes are missing.
